{"review_id": "iclr_HJeOMhA5K7_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_HJeOMhA5K7", "passages": [{"quote": "The method does not make major changes to the network structure", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty of network structure"}, {"quote": "the form of knowledge is limited and simple", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "knowledge representation capability"}, {"quote": "Experiments have shown that the convergence speed and results are improved, but not significant", "polarity": "mixed", "aspect": "experimental improvement magnitude"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_HJeOMhA5K7_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_HJeOMhA5K7", "passages": [{"quote": "The  problem  is  quite  interesting  and  is  practical  in  real-world.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "problem significance"}, {"quote": "the improvement (which I trust is real) depends critically on the quality and quantity of the human-crafted rules", "polarity": "mixed", "aspect": "method generalizability"}, {"quote": "The  presentation  of  datasets  consumes  a  lot  of  space  and  can  be  reduced", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "presentation efficiency"}, {"quote": "This  paper  displays  many  unnecessary  figures  that  consumes  a  lot  of  space.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "figure utility"}, {"quote": "The  paper  provides  some  unnecessary  text  highlights  in  bold.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "text formatting choices"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_HJeOMhA5K7_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_HJeOMhA5K7", "passages": [{"quote": "The authors find a fresh direction for learning with noisy samples.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "research direction novelty"}, {"quote": "The authors perform numerical experiments to demonstrate the efficacy of their framework.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental demonstration"}, {"quote": "their experimental result support their previous claims.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "claim validation"}, {"quote": "The authors are encouraged to re-write their paper with more motivated storyline. The current version is okay but not very exciting for idea selling.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "motivation and presentation"}, {"quote": "you may not restrict your general method into ColumnNet, which will limit the practical usage.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "method generality"}]}
{"review_id": "ANCH-2", "paper_id": "ANCH-2", "passages": [{"quote": "This submission provides a rigorous theoretical analysis; the proofs appear correct and the assumptions are clearly stated.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "theoretical rigor"}, {"quote": "My main concern is reproducibility: no code is provided and several hyperparameters are unreported.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "reproducibility"}, {"quote": "The related-work coverage is adequate.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "related work coverage"}, {"quote": "Overall the significance for the broader community seems modest.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "broader significance"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_SJGvns0qK7_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_SJGvns0qK7", "passages": [{"quote": "The idea behind the algorithm proposed in the paper is quite simple.", "polarity": "mixed", "aspect": "algorithmic novelty"}, {"quote": "The structure of the paper could be improved significantly. Four pages have been dedicated to the preliminaries and related work, and another four pages to the experiments.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "paper structure"}, {"quote": "I personally would like to see more discussion on how the distribution over MDPs is updated.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "explanation completeness"}, {"quote": "I did not find the experiments very convincing.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "experimental convincingness"}, {"quote": "the proposed algorithm performs similarly to the adaptive policy gradient method", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "performance advantage"}, {"quote": "the algorithms selected for comparison are not the right algorithms for POMDPs", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "baseline selection"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_SJGvns0qK7_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_SJGvns0qK7", "passages": [{"quote": "The main part of the paper is trying to explain Bayesian RL and the relationship between BAMDP and POMDP, and several related work. There is only a half page that explains the main idea of the proposed method", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "content balance"}, {"quote": "it seems that the author combines several existing techniques and utilize deep learning to solve BAMDP and POMDP problems.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "technical novelty"}, {"quote": "The detail of the experiment is not clarified explicitly", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "experimental detail"}, {"quote": "I am not sure that whether the novelty of this paper is enough for the main conference track.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty sufficiency"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_SJGvns0qK7_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_SJGvns0qK7", "passages": [{"quote": "the paper is well written. Related work are thoroughly discussed.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "writing and related work"}, {"quote": "the proposed idea is a solid combination of existing techniques", "polarity": "mixed", "aspect": "novelty"}, {"quote": "this combination is still worth trying and has been shown to scale to larger problems through the use of deep learning.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "scalability"}, {"quote": "Root sampling (step 3 in Algorithm 1) would result in sampled models that are fixed in every simulation.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "algorithmic design concern"}, {"quote": "Finely discretized belief would increase the complexity and computation dramatically with the dimension of the latent space.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "computational complexity"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_SJGvns0qK7_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_SJGvns0qK7", "passages": [{"quote": "This is a solid paper: The idea is clear, it is well communicated and put into context of the existing literature, and the results are promising.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "overall quality"}, {"quote": "The experiments are well chosen and illustrate the method well.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental design"}, {"quote": "The connection between the chosen setting (BAMDPs) to POMDPs is explained well and explored in the empirical evaluation as well.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "conceptual clarity"}, {"quote": "I think that the methods section could go into a bit more detail, and the underlying assumptions that the authors make could be discussed more critically.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "detail and critical discussion"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_H1z-PsR5KX_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_H1z-PsR5KX", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper is well-written and provides valuable information to understand the behaviour of neural machine translation models.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "writing and value"}, {"quote": "The ability to control characteristics (such as gender) without training specialized models is promising, even if the results are not good enough for immediate use.", "polarity": "mixed", "aspect": "control capability"}, {"quote": "Multiple NMT systems are necessary to discover important neurons.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "method requirement"}, {"quote": "The findings in this paper do not lead to immediate translation performance improvements.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "practical impact"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_H1z-PsR5KX_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_H1z-PsR5KX", "passages": [{"quote": "even though the methods for detecting important neurons are not novel (as also stated in the paper), their application to MT is novel", "polarity": "mixed", "aspect": "method and application novelty"}, {"quote": "the presentation is very clear", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "presentation clarity"}, {"quote": "the choice of methods is well argued and justified", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "methodological justification"}, {"quote": "the experiments are well executed and analysed", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental quality"}, {"quote": "thorough and varied analysis of the experimental findings", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "analysis thoroughness"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_H1z-PsR5KX_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_H1z-PsR5KX", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper is very well written and provides solid intuitions for the methods proposed.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "writing and intuition"}, {"quote": "The methods seem promising, and the degree of localist representation is striking.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "method promise"}, {"quote": "There is a correlation between the neuron importance metrics proposed in the paper and the effect on BLEU score of erasing those neurons from the network", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "metric validity"}, {"quote": "It wasn't clear to me why the neurons that track particular properties couldn't be identified using a supervised classifier to begin with", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "methodological necessity"}, {"quote": "most of the insight in the paper seems to be derived from the supervised experiments.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "contribution source"}, {"quote": "The particular linguistic properties that are being investigated in the classification experiments are fairly limited.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "scope of investigation"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_Syxgbh05tQ_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_Syxgbh05tQ", "passages": [{"quote": "The proposed Lyapunov-function based approach for policy optimization is certainly appealing and the derived algorithms make sense to me.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "method appeal"}, {"quote": "This paper provides a solid contribution to the safe RL literature", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "contribution significance"}, {"quote": "the contribution is solid but seems to be of somewhat incremental nature to me, combining existing recent techniques", "polarity": "mixed", "aspect": "novelty"}, {"quote": "the experimental results do not seem to show a drastic benefit over the Lagrangian baselines.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "experimental results"}, {"quote": "the experiments are based on extensive grid search over hyper-parameters including learning rates and regularization parameters.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "experimental methodology"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_Syxgbh05tQ_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_Syxgbh05tQ", "passages": [{"quote": "the novelty of the approach is questionable, not only in light of recent papers but older literature", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty"}, {"quote": "the actual tasks chosen are quite simple and do not present complex instabilities.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "task complexity"}, {"quote": "actually creating a Lyapunov function and weighing the relative magnitude of its second derivative (steep/shallow) is not trivial", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "implementation difficulty"}, {"quote": "comparison of CPO and Lagrangian constraint based RL with Lyapunov based method proposed depends on a lot of factors that are not systematically explored by the paper.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "experimental completeness"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_Syxgbh05tQ_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_Syxgbh05tQ", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper is very well written (a few typos here and there, please revise) and structured, and, to the best of my knowledge, it is technically sound and very detailed.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "writing and technical quality"}, {"quote": "It provides incremental advances, mostly from Chow et al., 2018.", "polarity": "mixed", "aspect": "novelty"}, {"quote": "It fairly accounts for recent literature in the field.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "related work coverage"}, {"quote": "Experimental settings and results are fairly convincing.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental quality"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_Syxgbh05tQ_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_Syxgbh05tQ", "passages": [{"quote": "this work seems like an interesting framework for encompassing several classes of constrained policy optimization settings in the Lyapunov-based setting", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "framework generality"}, {"quote": "I have some concerns about the evaluation methodology.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "evaluation methodology"}, {"quote": "The original method has been modified to form a new baseline and I'm not sure that it is 'without loss of generality'.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "baseline fairness"}, {"quote": "it is unclear whether the results can be accepted at face value. Are these averaged across several random seeds and trials?", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "statistical rigor"}, {"quote": "Recent work has shown that taking 1 run especially in MuJoCo environments doesn't necessarily provide statistically significant values.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "result reliability"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_B1e7hs05Km_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_B1e7hs05Km", "passages": [{"quote": "Introduction and preliminaries section give useful background context and motivation. I found it easy to follow despite not having much hands-on background in RL.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "accessibility and context"}, {"quote": "Proposes a novel (to my knowledge) exploration method for RL which intuitively seems like it should work better", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty"}, {"quote": "The method looks simple to implement on top of existing Q-learning based methods and has minimal computational and memory costs.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "implementation simplicity"}, {"quote": "Strong empirical performance as compared with appropriate baselines", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical performance"}, {"quote": "Good discussion of practical implementation issues (architecture, hyperparameters, etc.) in Appendix A.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "implementation detail"}, {"quote": "I don't understand the Theorem statement (let alone the proof) or what it tells me about the proposed BDQN algorithm.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "theoretical clarity"}, {"quote": "there's a common abuse of big-O notation here that should be fixed for a formal statement", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "notation precision"}, {"quote": "much of the writing seems quite rushed with many typos and grammatical errors throughout.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "writing quality"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_B1e7hs05Km_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_B1e7hs05Km", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper looks very promising because of a relatively simple methodology (in the positive sense) and impressive results", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "methodology and results"}, {"quote": "I find the paper having big issues with clarity. There are so many mistakes, typos, unclear statements and a questionable structure in the text", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity and structure"}, {"quote": "In the current version the paper is not ready for publication.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "publication readiness"}]}
{"review_id": "ANCH-1", "paper_id": "ANCH-1", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper tackles an interesting problem.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "problem significance"}, {"quote": "the novelty is limited: the proposed method is a straightforward combination of two existing techniques.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty"}, {"quote": "The writing is also difficult to follow in Sections 3-4, with undefined notation.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "writing clarity"}, {"quote": "the experimental evaluation is thorough, covering five datasets with proper ablations.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental thoroughness"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_B1e7hs05Km_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_B1e7hs05Km", "passages": [{"quote": "Simple and elegant algorithm.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "algorithm design"}, {"quote": "Strong empirical results in standard benchmarks.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "empirical results"}, {"quote": "The paper is very poorly written; the number of typos is countless, and in general the paper is quite hard to read and to follow.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "writing quality"}, {"quote": "I share the concerns expressed in the first public comment regarding the correctness of the theoretical statements (Theorem 1) or, at least, the proposed proofs.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "theoretical correctness"}, {"quote": "I think Table 1, Figure 1, and Figure 2 are not particularly useful and could be removed.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "figure utility"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_B1e7hs05Km_r4", "paper_id": "iclr_B1e7hs05Km", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper presents some strong experimental results.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental results"}, {"quote": "The novelty of the method falls a little short for a full-scale conference paper. After all, it is only a special case of [3]", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "novelty"}, {"quote": "the paper should have definitely provided a comparison against [3].", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "baseline comparison"}, {"quote": "It is hard to conclude much from the fact that the proposed method outperforms DDQN, which is by design not meant for sample efficiency", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "experimental interpretation"}, {"quote": "Key citations to very closely related prior work are missing, for instance [1,2].", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "related work coverage"}, {"quote": "The paper has excessively many typos and misspellings.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "writing quality"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_ryeYpJSKwr_r0", "paper_id": "iclr_ryeYpJSKwr", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper is well written and it proposes a novel direction for research.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "writing and novelty"}, {"quote": "the authors should look further inside their newly designed acquisition functions, not merely treat them as black boxes.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "analysis depth"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_ryeYpJSKwr_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_ryeYpJSKwr", "passages": [{"quote": "the proposed method makes sense and would benefit from further experimental ablation.", "polarity": "mixed", "aspect": "method soundness"}, {"quote": "Using RL to automatically derive (N)AFs is a nice change of pace from the hand-crafted heuristics that dominate BO. I like the ideas at play here", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "methodological approach"}, {"quote": "I am not yet convinced that NAFs learn representations that go beyond standard AFs combined with a prior over $x$.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "contribution significance"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_ryeYpJSKwr_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_ryeYpJSKwr", "passages": [{"quote": "The paper is mostly clearly written and I am not aware of existing work on meta-learning the AF for BO.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "writing and novelty"}, {"quote": "the approach is related to Chen et al, which is cited in the text but not used as a baseline.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "baseline comparison"}, {"quote": "It is also not shown clearly enough how the performance of MetaBO depends on the number of training tasks and distance between training and test tasks.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "experimental analysis"}, {"quote": "the performance improvements are marginal (less than 1.0 on three datasets, except QUASAR-T", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "performance improvement magnitude"}, {"quote": "there is a very related work... which also proposes a new pretraining approach... Not only this submission did not discuss this paper... the result is substantially worse", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "related work and comparative performance"}, {"quote": "the paper does not discuss any work in question generation overall, although the task of question generation was studied for decades", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "related work coverage"}, {"quote": "it looks like the paper uses the development set for both development and the final evaluation.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "experimental methodology"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_H1lFsREYPS_r0", "paper_id": "iclr_H1lFsREYPS", "passages": [{"quote": "Overall the paper is written rather well, however,  at times  it is tough  to understand because of the technical writing and heavy use of abbreviations.", "polarity": "mixed", "aspect": "writing clarity"}, {"quote": "The experiments make sense given the research question.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental design"}, {"quote": "How often where these experiments repeated? What are the standard errors?", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "statistical rigor"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_H1lFsREYPS_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_H1lFsREYPS", "passages": [{"quote": "The idea in the paper is new and interesting, and they provide a good intuition of why the proposed learning objective is helpful compared to the previous methods.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty and intuition"}, {"quote": "the performance improvements are marginal (less than 1.0 on three datasets, except QUASAR-T, which is actually interesting given it is under transfer learning setting).", "polarity": "mixed", "aspect": "performance improvement magnitude"}, {"quote": "there is a very related work... which also proposes a new pretraining approach for question generation and data augmentation... Not only this submission did not discuss this paper... the result is substantially worse", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "related work and comparative performance"}, {"quote": "the paper does not discuss any work in question generation overall, although the task of question generation was studied for decades", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "related work coverage"}, {"quote": "it looks like the paper uses the development set for both development and the final evaluation.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "experimental methodology"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_m4PC1eUknQG_r0", "paper_id": "iclr_m4PC1eUknQG", "passages": [{"quote": "OSG removes the requirement of preparing the population or task distribution in meta-learning, which can be expensive.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "efficiency"}, {"quote": "Section 3.3.1 shows promising results that the proposed MMD regularization term can generate diverse opponents.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental validation"}, {"quote": "OSG, which generates a competitive and diverse opponent population, is a paper's main contribution. However, this paper compares the baselines trained based on the random opponent population", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "baseline appropriateness"}, {"quote": "the experimental results do not seem to show a drastic benefit over the Lagrangian baselines.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "performance advantage"}, {"quote": "it is not clear why the initialization of the Lagrange multiplier for the Lagrangian baselines was chosen fixed.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "experimental fairness"}, {"quote": "hyper-parameters/training details for L2E and the baselines (e.g., the number of trajectories for each adaptation) are missing.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "reproducibility"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_m4PC1eUknQG_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_m4PC1eUknQG", "passages": [{"quote": "This paper is tackling a very relevant, interesting and difficult problem.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "problem significance"}, {"quote": "I find the general approach of optimizing a policy to be able to 'rapidly' and exploit a broad range of opponents to be very exciting.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "approach appeal"}, {"quote": "To the best of my (admittedly limited) knowledge, the suggested approach is significantly novel.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "novelty"}, {"quote": "the diversity-inducing regularization term, using the MMD over the distribution of trajectories induced by the policies is interesting and potentially has a broader applicability", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "technical contribution"}, {"quote": "several key points remain unclear to me. Most notably, after training of L2E and when facing opponents with unknown policies, how does the base policy adapts?", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "clarity"}, {"quote": "it looks (to me, because no comment is made about it in the manuscript) like L2E must scale terribly with the size of the action space.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "scalability"}, {"quote": "A point is made, several times in the manuscript, that the base policy becomes 'more robust and eliminates its weaknesses'... it is not really clear what is precisely meant by this.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "conceptual clarity"}, {"quote": "I find that the writing could also be improved. While the algorithm is admittedly hard to fully describe in a very succinct way, the amount of repetions or redundancies in the first 6 pages", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "writing quality"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_m4PC1eUknQG_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_m4PC1eUknQG", "passages": [{"quote": "I think there is a collection of ideas here that are publishable and are of interest to the community.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "contribution significance"}, {"quote": "Having a diversity regularized policy optimization procedure with MMD is interesting.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "methodological contribution"}, {"quote": "The PG update rules are interesting.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "technical contribution"}, {"quote": "I am unsure about some of the claims wrt implicit/explicit opponent modelling.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "conceptual clarity"}, {"quote": "The MMD term seems very expensive and I am not sure it will scale, particularly with population size.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "scalability"}, {"quote": "I would like to see more details on the actual training. How many outer and inner iterations were needed to converge?", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "experimental detail"}, {"quote": "The results in Figure 2 do not seem to match up with the numbers in Table 1.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "result consistency"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_m4PC1eUknQG_r3", "paper_id": "iclr_m4PC1eUknQG", "passages": [{"quote": "motivation, solution, novelty, and overall presentation were almost clear", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "clarity"}, {"quote": "the implementation details were unclear and there were no shared codes.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "reproducibility"}, {"quote": "I think the idea contributed to this community", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "contribution"}, {"quote": "the results of two poker games and one grid soccer game indicate that L2E quickly adapts to diverse styles of unknown opponents.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental results"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_m08OHhXxl-5_r0", "paper_id": "iclr_m08OHhXxl-5", "passages": [{"quote": "Addresses a new, interesting, and practically relevant problem.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "problem significance"}, {"quote": "Technically strong, good insights and clearly bridges the gap between two distinct areas.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "technical quality"}, {"quote": "Well organized and written, very clear for the most part.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "writing quality"}, {"quote": "The sensitivity of f cannot be bounded. What the authors propose (Section C.2.1) to address this... is not generally accepted.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "theoretical soundness"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_m08OHhXxl-5_r1", "paper_id": "iclr_m08OHhXxl-5", "passages": [{"quote": "The empirical results seem complete.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental completeness"}, {"quote": "The proposed algorithm is not described very clearly in section 3 and section 4. After spending considerable time reading sections 3 and 4, I still feel hard to follow", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "algorithmic clarity"}, {"quote": "The privacy part seems like a plug-and-play of the Laplace mechanism. Hence, the technical novelty might be limited.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "technical novelty"}, {"quote": "the calculation of sensitivity seems to be wrong. As the authors claim in Section C.2.1 in the appendix, the sensitivity is technically infinite.", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "technical correctness"}]}
{"review_id": "iclr_m08OHhXxl-5_r2", "paper_id": "iclr_m08OHhXxl-5", "passages": [{"quote": "The use of accuracy temperature scaling is neat in combination with DP. Whilst not a startling novelty, it is a nice observation that their method combines so well with differential privacy", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "methodological fit"}, {"quote": "Strong experimental section. Although only on image data, the experiments cover a multitude of shift types, and the baselines are apt for the task.", "polarity": "pos", "aspect": "experimental coverage"}, {"quote": "In terms of methodology, the paper is only tangentially related to domain shift, since there is a form of fine-tuning on the target dataset", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "methodological alignment"}, {"quote": "there must also be an interplay between the degree of shift, the effectiveness of transfer learning and calibration. This is not really covered", "polarity": "neg", "aspect": "analysis completeness"}]}
